#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:2
msgid "``expr`` tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:4
msgid ""
"**Expr tasks** consist of a single `Python expression <https://docs.python."
"org/3/reference/expressions.html>`_. Running the task evaluates the "
"expression and outputs the resulting value. Here's a trivial example of an "
"expr task that will print `2` when run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:6
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.trivial-example]\n"
"expr = \"1 + 1\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:11
msgid ""
"$ poe trivial-example\n"
"Poe => 1 + 1\n"
"2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:17
msgid "**Expressions can:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:19
msgid ""
"use most Python expression constructs with the exception of yield, await, or "
"named expressions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:21
msgid ""
"use most builtin functions including all members of `this collection "
"<https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/blob/main/poethepoet/helpers/python."
"py#L13>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:23
msgid ""
"reference the |sys_module_link| module without having to specify it as an "
"import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:131
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html\" target=\"_blank\">sys "
"module</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:24
msgid ""
"directly access whatever arguments were passed to the task from `sys.argv`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:25
msgid ""
"reference values of named args as Python variables with a Python type "
"matching the configured arg type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:26
msgid ""
"include environment variables as string values that are injected into the "
"expression using the usual templating syntax ``${...}``, including the :ref:"
"`default and alternate value operators <parameter-expansion-operators>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:30
msgid "Available task options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:32
msgid ""
"``expr`` tasks support all of the :doc:`standard task options <../options>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:34
msgid "The following options are also accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:36
msgid ""
"**imports** : ``list[str]`` :ref:`📖<Referencing imported modules in an "
"expression>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:35
msgid "list[str] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:37
msgid "A list of modules to import for use in the expression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:39
msgid ""
"**assert** : ``bool`` :ref:`📖<Fail if the expression result is falsey>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:38
msgid "bool 📖"
msgstr "bool 📖"

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:40
msgid ""
"If set to true and the result of the expression is found to be a falsey "
"value then the task will fail with a non-zero return value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:42
msgid ""
"**ignore_fail** : ``bool`` | ``list[int]``  :ref:`📖<Ignore task failure>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:41
msgid "bool | list[int]  📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:43
msgid ""
"Return exit code 0 even if the task fails, or specify a list of task exit "
"codes to ignore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:47
msgid "Referencing arguments and environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:49
msgid ""
"The expression can reference environment variables using templating syntax "
"as in :doc:`cmd<cmd>` tasks, and named arguments as Python variables in "
"scope as in :doc:`script<script>` tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:51
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.venv-active]\n"
"expr = \"\"\"(\n"
"  f'{target_venv} is active'\n"
"  if '${VIRTUAL_ENV}'.endswith(target_venv)\n"
"  else f'{target_venv} is not active'\n"
")\"\"\"\n"
"args = [{ name = \"target-venv\", default = \".venv\", positional = true }]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:61
msgid ""
"$ poe venv-active poethepoet-LCpCQf8S-py3.10\n"
"Poe => (\n"
"  f'{target_venv} is active'\n"
"  if '${VIRTUAL_ENV}'.endswith(target_venv)\n"
"  else f'{target_venv} is not active'\n"
")\n"
"poethepoet-LCpCQf8S-py3.10 is not active"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:71
msgid ""
"In this example the ``VIRTUAL_ENV`` environment variable is templated into "
"the expression using the usual templating syntax, and the ``target_venv`` "
"argument is referenced directly as a variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:73
msgid ""
"Notice that the expression may be formatted over multiple lines, as in "
"normal python code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:77
msgid "Referencing imported modules in an expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:79
msgid ""
"By default the sys module is available to the expression which allows access "
"to ``sys.argv`` or ``sys.platform`` among other useful values. However you "
"can also reference any other importable Python module via the imports option "
"as in the following example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:81
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.count-hidden]\n"
"help    = \"Count hidden files or subdirectories\"\n"
"expr    = \"len(list(pathlib.Path('.').glob('.*')))\"\n"
"imports = [\"pathlib\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:90
msgid "Fail if the expression result is falsey"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:92
msgid ""
"The expression can be made to behave like an assertion that fails if the "
"result is not truthy by providing the assert option. The task defined in the "
"following example will return non-zero if the result is False."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:95
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.venv-active]\n"
"expr   = \"${VIRTUAL_ENV}.endswith(target_venv)\"\n"
"assert = true\n"
"args   = [{ name = \"target-venv\", default = \".venv\", positional = true }]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:104
msgid "Referencing the result of other tasks in an expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:106
msgid ""
"Expr tasks can reference the results of other tasks by leveraging the :doc:"
"`uses <../../guides/composition_guide>` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:108
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks._get_active_session]\n"
"cmd = \"read_session --format json\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.show-user]\n"
"expr    = \"\"\"(\n"
"  f\"User: {json.loads(${SESSION_JSON})['User']}\"\n"
"  if len(${SESSION_JSON}) > 2\n"
"  else \"No active session.\"\n"
")\"\"\"\n"
"uses    = { SESSION_JSON = \"_get_active_session\" }\n"
"imports = [\"json\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:124
msgid "Accessing free arguments via ``_extra_args``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:126
msgid ""
"Free arguments (arguments not matched by any named arg definition, or "
"arguments passed after :sh:`--`) are available inside expr tasks as the "
"``_extra_args`` variable — a ``list[str]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/expr.rst:128
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`forwarding-free-arguments-via-poe-extra-args` section of the "
"args guide for details and examples."
msgstr ""
